cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below, and cite the
  accompanying manuscript and data record listed in the README.
type: software
title: "oncophenomap: genotype-phenotype maps and tree-based variance decomposition"
abstract: >-
  oncophenomap is a Python library for constructing tree-based genotype-phenotype maps
  from a reduced phenotype space and a set of genomic features. It fits genotype-driven
  partitions of the phenotype space, optionally after residualizing on chromosome-arm and
  H&E context, quantifies the variance explained by the fitted tree, and builds group
  heatmaps for inspecting the resulting map.
